    section.page-section
        .container
            .row
                .col-lg-9
                    h3 Verification Protocol
                    h5.mt-4.mb-3 Title Search
                    p QANDOS conducts a comprehensive title search to confirm the legal ownership and transferability of every property. Our verification process reviews land registry records, title documents, and historical ownership to ensure the seller has the lawful right to transfer the asset. By identifying inconsistencies, incomplete transfers, or potential ownership disputes early, this step helps ensure that every verified property rests on a clear and legitimate legal foundation.

                    h5.mt-4.mb-3 Survey Verification
                    p Accurate land boundaries are essential to secure property ownership. QANDOS verifies survey plans and geospatial records to confirm that the property’s documented location, coordinates, and boundaries match official survey data. This process helps prevent issues such as overlapping claims, inaccurate boundary descriptions, or falsified survey documents—ensuring the land being purchased exists exactly where the records say it does.

                    h5.mt-4.mb-3 Developer Background Check
                    p Trust extends beyond the property to the people behind it. QANDOS conducts background checks on developers and sellers to evaluate their credibility, operational history, and track record within the real estate market. By reviewing corporate registration details, past developments, and market reputation, we help ensure buyers are dealing with legitimate professionals committed to delivering on their promises.

                    h5.mt-4.mb-3 Government Records Verification
                    p To confirm a property’s legitimacy within the formal land administration system, QANDOS reviews relevant government documentation and regulatory records. This step ensures the property aligns with official registrations and approvals, helping identify discrepancies between what is being offered and what exists in public records. The result is greater transparency and confidence for buyers navigating complex property documentation.

                    h5.mt-4.mb-3 Physical Inspection
                    p Documentation alone is not enough, properties must also be verified on the ground. QANDOS coordinates physical inspections to confirm the existence, location, and condition of the property being offered. By validating that the asset matches its documentation and listing details, this step helps identify misrepresentations and ensures buyers are investing in something that has been physically confirmed.

                    h5.mt-4.mb-3 Litigation Check
                    p Undisclosed legal disputes can significantly affect property ownership and transfer. QANDOS conducts litigation checks to identify whether a property is connected to ongoing legal claims, ownership disputes, or court proceedings. By bringing potential legal risks to light before a transaction proceeds, this process helps buyers make informed decisions and avoid properties that could become legally complicated.

                    h5.mt-4.mb-3 Escrow Setup
                    p For qualified transactions, QANDOS facilitates secure escrow arrangements to protect both buyers and sellers. Funds are held by a neutral third party and released only when agreed conditions, such as document verification and transfer requirements; have been met. This structure ensures transparency and accountability throughout the transaction, allowing both parties to complete the process with confidence.
